{"data":{"featured":{"nodes":[{"id":"b65b4af2-dd14-5665-920e-906d00bd6786","html":"<p>Built at Prof. Max Simchowitz's lab at CMU, DexterLab is a benchmark for training and evaluating generative dexterous policies on a UR5e arm and Allegro hand, modeled as a single 22-DoF system. Existing benchmarks treat the hand in isolation with a floating wrist; DexterLab co-optimizes arm and hand together. I built a Leap Motion teleoperation pipeline with QP-based arm IK and neural finger retargeting (GeoRT), trained flow-matching BC policies on ~10 minutes of demos, and used OGPO RL post-training to raise pick-and-place success from 30% to 64%.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"MaxLab · CMU","title":"DexterLab: Benchmarking Generative Dexterous Policies","tech":["MuJoCo","PyTorch","Flow Matching","RL","Leap Motion"],"github":null,"external":null,"cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#182838","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/ee256/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/d15ba/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/ee256/cover.jpg 700w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/5cc47/cover.jpg 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/5890a/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/8ceca/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/4a8e6587bd29a6983f3bda29842dc75f/f0297/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":394}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/30de0d932ee1a4a836d9931c60f2ed2c/video.mp4"}}},{"id":"35616607-0fbe-52de-841e-7eb40556d8ba","html":"<p>Implemented RL Token (RLT) on SmolVLA, compressing frozen VLM embeddings into a single token that conditions a lightweight TD3 actor-critic, so the policy improves through online RL without extra demonstrations. Validated the token with PCA and t-SNE, where last-step embeddings cleanly separate success from failure episodes, and raised Meta-World peg-insert success from 72% to 88% over the BC baseline.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"Intro to Deep Learning Course · CMU","title":"RL Post-Training of a Flow-Based VLA","tech":["SmolVLA","LeRobot","TD3","PyTorch","Meta-World"],"github":"https://github.com/a-daksh/RLT-lerobot","external":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1GTqD60x7lDk_GR6dy1xD2Gtjt3eG7BQ1?usp=sharing","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#787878","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/ee256/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/d15ba/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/ee256/cover.jpg 700w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/5890a/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/b94231e826b6251b7726af919f4e3812/8ceca/cover.webp 700w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":394}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/e6ba9940e2479f40b16310085d27192f/video.mp4"}}},{"id":"eb9cfdc6-d7b5-5719-bb55-77415faa8990","html":"<p>Built as part of the Deep Reinforcement Learning Control course at CMU, this project developed a hierarchical multi-agent framework for Neural MMO. The system trains specialist policies (Combat, Forage, Survival) via distributed self-play using IMPALA and composes them into a generalist agent using a Mixture-of-Experts approach. We trained using PPO and UPGO, outperforming all baselines to achieve 2nd place.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"Deep RL & Control Course · CMU","title":"MMOsaic: Combining Specialist Policies for Generalist Multi-Agent Play","tech":["Python","PyTorch","IMPALA","Distributed RL","MARL"],"github":"https://github.com/MMO-saic/","external":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1THEhzcVMJ8EumUixfRKF9vyV5RAXd-dU?usp=sharing","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#081818","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/ee256/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/d15ba/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/ee256/cover.jpg 700w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/5890a/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/af40234464b29d606e60210ae1c4c1d6/8ceca/cover.webp 700w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":394}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/c5526cb1e0127afda870a3d001c3d5a6/video.mp4"}}},{"id":"72fcf9f2-4902-5564-977e-bb8cdf3641f4","html":"<p>The project aims to address the limitations of Total Knee Arthroplasty by integrating AR with robot assisted manipulation, enhancing surgical visualization and procedural accuracy. The system provides functionality to overlay a surgical plan on the patient’s anatomy using the Apple Vision Pro headset, while a KUKA LBR MED7 robotic arm is used to screw surgical pins into bones with sub-centimeter precision (2mm and 2°).</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"MRSD Capstone · CMU","title":"Bone.P.A.R.T.E","tech":["Python","C++","Swift","ROS2","MoveIT2","SAM","DinoV3"],"github":"https://github.com/KNEEpoleon","external":"https://mrsdprojects.ri.cmu.edu/2025teamd/","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#887868","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/ee256/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/d15ba/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/ee256/cover.jpg 700w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/5cc47/cover.jpg 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/5890a/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/8ceca/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/5cacf07d8a791320702be52bb75180e3/f0297/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":394}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/dcad9adaedf0b1fd90e719528dfab1e5/video.mp4"}}},{"id":"d349fa88-8731-50fd-9f61-20d7d92835f5","html":"<p>Built for the CMU Vision-Language-Autonomy Challenge (IROS 2025), this project developed a Vision-Language Navigation system combining Gemini 2.5 Pro's embodied reasoning with a custom ROS state machine. The system intelligently resolves spatial queries (e.g., \"closest to the window\") to produce object references and waypoint plans under a strict 10-minute limit. The entire stack was containerized via Docker for reliable deployment on real robot hardware, achieving 3rd place in the competition.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"CMU VLA Challenge · IROS 2025","title":"CMU Vision Language Autonomy Challenge","tech":["Python","ROS","Gemini 2.5 Pro","Docker"],"github":"https://github.com/a-daksh/Hierarchical-VLM-for-Vision-Language-Navigation","external":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1OA9SbvrHb39ljxXzefxj5CtzCdYZuzCI?usp=drive_link","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#080808","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/4892d/cover.png","srcSet":"/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/6e655/cover.png 175w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/2ebaa/cover.png 350w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/4892d/cover.png 700w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/2299d/cover.png 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/c1ac9/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/8e261/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/a3004/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/8460d9a403ede32555c33136d38f254e/1fa20/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":427}}},"video":null}},{"id":"96b1ba5d-9d0d-57b0-9725-a8f5e7dfa058","html":"<p>Built as part of the Optimal Control and Reinforcement Learning course at CMU, this project simulated a penalty-style soccer kick using the Unitree G1 humanoid. The system computed the required impulse to strike the ball toward a target, generated a feasible motion with direct collocation, and used infinite-horizon LQR for balancing along with time-varying LQR for trajectory tracking.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"Optimal Control & RL Course · CMU","title":"Unitree G1 Soccer Ball Kicking","tech":["Julia","IHLQR","TVLQR","QP","DIRCOL"],"github":"https://github.com/a-daksh/16745_Unitree_G1_Goal_Kicking","external":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1bkAzpjAIa1z8fcTbUcF7YR9m2Zbwwave?usp=sharing","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#486898","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/ee256/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/d15ba/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/ee256/cover.jpg 700w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/5890a/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/f4983cd96282d5e31d245aa7c30304d0/8ceca/cover.webp 700w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":394}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/d167be6783ca89f5c60362ec922f7230/video.mp4"}}},{"id":"d6911be0-771b-50af-9193-60b0a1c807b4","html":"<p>Built as part of the Robot Autonomy course at CMU, this project used a Franka Emika Panda arm with a stamping mechanism to autonomously generate pixel art. The system converts images into grid patterns, optimizes stamping order with Christofides’ algorithm to minimize travel, and uses force-controlled stamping with ArUco tagged ink pads for adaptability.</p>","frontmatter":{"label":"Robot Autonomy Course · CMU","title":"Stamp Pixel Art Using a Franka Arm","tech":["ROS1","Python","FrankaPy"],"github":"https://github.com/a-daksh/pixel-art-franka","external":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fLW2rSwOEIGwB48E1Zd0QJzGh6RTqoWj?usp=sharing","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","backgroundColor":"#080808","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/24c0a/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/834b4/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/d25f7/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/24c0a/cover.jpg 700w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/f9c42/cover.jpg 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/0823c/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/919bf/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/c7a9c/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/632fb07c132163b224264cb5c85d654a/36a94/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":393}}},"video":{"publicURL":"/static/9b9853ea6767e9cbe0869f999ba6fe41/video.mp4"}}}]}}}